{
  "schema_version": 2,
  "_note": "Vendored binary pins, PER PLATFORM. Each tool's `assets` map is keyed by <os>-<arch>; `binary` is the base name and Windows adds .exe. Checksums are recorded by `python tools/third_party.py --pin <tool> [--platform <p>]` (trust-on-first-use against the upstream release asset) and verified on every init thereafter. Pinning downloads WITHOUT executing, so ONE machine can pin every platform. An unpinned platform fails closed and is named -- a silently absent tool is indistinguishable from a tool that ran and found nothing. Non-Windows asset_patterns are unverified until their first --pin, which fails loudly with the real asset names if a pattern is wrong. Re-pins land via reviewed PR. Verification is sha256 and nothing else: `--verify` re-hashes each installed binary and compares it against the digest recorded when it was pinned. It runs offline, under Tier 0's no-network promise.",
